<<~ ahu slot=`#/invitation`>>
! Example Four ~ a component whose success depends on the next image

```tiddlywiki
<<art worktype=`isolated atmospheric overlay for an existing composition` subject=`passing bands of luminous haze` read=`soft depth that leaves the underlying picture intelligible` imagery=`a few uneven veils of delicate color with large untouched intervals` treatment=`diffuse watercolor-like diffusion and gentle edge falloff` composition=`asymmetric partial coverage with broad clear margins` relation=`modulates the unseen base image without replacing its subjects or lettering` depiction-scope=`only the overlay component; no complete scene, page, or studio setup`>>
```
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/artifact-example`>>
The Art Sigil does not itself ensure actual transparent pixels. A companion artifact contract could independently require RGBA output, transparent corners and a measured alpha channel, with no unrequested background.

```toml
[artifact]
role = "overlay"
canvas_px = [512, 512]
format = "PNG/RGBA"
pixel_alpha = "required: all designated clear margins alpha 0"
registration = "same canvas origin as a separately identified base"
test = "inspect alpha and composite at intended display scale"
```

If the receiver supplies opaque watercolor-like material, that may serve as a color reference but fails the technical overlay contract. A masking/postproduction step can correct the artifact, provided it is named as an intervention.
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/noninheritance`>>
This case does not make transparency, pixel dimensions, watercolor, layer stacks, or rectangular canvases requirements of all artworks.
<<~/ahu>>

